meta {
  name: Create Provider (Embedding - Mistral)
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/ai_provider_configs
  body: json
  auth: basic
}

auth:basic {
  username: {{admin_username}}
  password: {{admin_password}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/ld+json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "openrouter-embed-recruteurs",
    "usage": "embedding",
    "provider": "api_endpoint",
    "apiEndpoint": "https://api.mistral.ai/v1/embeddings",
    "apiKey": "{{mistral_api_key}}",
    "model": "mistral-embed",
    "isActive": true,
    "isDefault": true
  }
}

docs {
  Cloud/free-tier alternative to "Create Provider (Embedding)" (Ollama +
  mxbai-embed-large, dimension 1024). Despite the row's `name` (kept as
  "openrouter-embed-recruteurs" for historical/DB continuity), this does NOT
  go through OpenRouter -- as of 2026-08-28, `GET
  https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models` shows OpenRouter's catalog has zero
  embedding models (no model has "embedding" in
  `architecture.output_modalities`, none have "embed" in their id); an
  earlier version of this request used
  "liquid/lfm-2.5-embedding-350m:free" against OpenRouter's
  /chat/completions-derived /embeddings endpoint
  (OpenAiCompatibleEmbeddingClient), but that model no longer exists in
  OpenRouter's catalog either.

  Reconfigured to hit **Mistral AI directly**: `apiEndpoint:
  https://api.mistral.ai/v1/embeddings`, `model: mistral-embed`. Still uses
  `provider: api_endpoint` / OpenAiCompatibleEmbeddingClient (Mistral's
  embeddings endpoint is OpenAI-compatible) -- only the target host and
  model changed, not the provider type or client implementation.
  `mistral-embed` natively outputs 1024-dimension vectors, matching
  VectorIndex.dimension / QdrantClient::VECTOR_SIZE for the existing Qdrant
  Cloud collection `cv_maxime_jolivet` with no resize/reindex needed.
  `{{mistral_api_key}}` is a Mistral AI API key (console.mistral.ai), not an
  OpenRouter one -- add it to your local Bruno environment.

  IMPORTANT: the embedding provider used to index a document and the one used
  to embed a query at search time MUST be the same model -- different models'
  vectors are not comparable even at the same dimension. If you change this
  provider later, reprocess every already-indexed document (see "Reprocess
  Document") or searches will silently degrade to near-random.
}
